        ":question/id": "09c9c63d-0730-53db-aef4-1a9fdd4918cb",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int (\\frac{1}{x+5}+\\frac{1}{x-5})\\,\\text{d}x.$ Assume that $K$ is an arbitrary positive constant.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's solve this using the general formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{x+5}+\\frac{1}{x-5})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x+5|+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x-5|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|(x+5)(x-5)|+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(K|(x+5)(x-5)|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the laws of logarithms to write the result as a single logarithm.",
